# Build output (huge)
release/

# rcedit, Resource Hacker, gh CLI, and similar third-party tools —
# fetched per-machine (see scripts/package.bat for download URLs)
tools/*.exe
tools/reshacker/
tools/gh/

# Build/fetch/package logs — scratch output from a single machine's run
*.log

# License secret artifacts — must NEVER be committed. gen-license-secret.py
# writes .profile_key here and the .h sibling lives in the chromium fork
# checkout (we keep a defensive line for it too in case the repo path
# changes). Plaintext profile JSONs stay tracked in this source repo for
# dev convenience; the release-zip packager (make-package.ps1) is what
# decides to ship .json.enc instead.
config/.profile_key
include/license_secret.h
# Encrypted release artifacts — produced by encrypt-profiles.py from the
# tracked plaintext JSONs. Re-derivable; don't pollute git history.
config/profiles/*.json.enc

# gen-token.exe has the license secret compiled in (same reason as
# .profile_key above) — make-package.ps1 rebuilds it fresh from the
# current .profile_key on every package run; scripts/gen-token-source.ps1
# (the template, no real secret in it) is what stays tracked.
scripts/gen-token.exe
scripts/gen-token*.cs

# OS junk
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.tmp
